AUC is the representation of the degree or measure of separability and is used as a summary of the Root Receiver Operator Characteristic (ROC) curve, which is curve is a visualisation graph representing imputation performance [143]. The AUC is represented by the true positive rate (TPR) and the false positive rate (FPR). Where the TPR is the proportion of correctly imputed positives of all positives and the TPR is the proportion of all negatives that are wrongly imputed as positives [144]. The true positive rate and the false positive rate are defined as:21\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
